ents with eating disorders.", "NIVELES DE VITAMINAS:Vitamin levels are assessed to monitor nutritional deficiencies that can arise in patients with eating disorders.", "AMILASA SÉRICA:Serum amylase levels are tested to evaluate pancreatic function, which can be affected by eating disorders.", "ESTUDIOS DEL TRACTO GASTROINTESTINAL:Gastrointestinal studies are conducted to assess digestive health and complications in patients with eating disorders.", "TC CRANEAL:Cranial CT scan is used to assess brain health and detect any complications related to eating disorders.", "ECOCARDIOGRAMA:Echocardiogram is used to assess heart structure and function, which can be affected by eating disorders.)<|COMPLETE|>", "EDUCATIONAL INSTITUTION:An institution that may provide psychological and nutritional education to patients recovering from eating disorders.", "ALCALOSIS METABÓLICA HIPOCLOREMICA:Alcalosis metabólica hipoclorémica is a metabolic disorder that can occur in patients with Bulimia Nervosa as a result of vomiting.", "AMENORREA:Amenorrhea is defined as the absence of menstruation and can manifest in two forms: primary and secondary. This condition is often observed in individuals with Anorexia Nervosa, where it is primarily linked to hormonal imbalances. In patients suffering from Anorexia Nervosa, the disruption of normal hormonal function can lead to the cessation of menstrual cycles, highlighting the significant impact of this eating disorder on reproductive health.", "EDUCACIÓN PSICOLÓGICA:Psicological education is crucial for patients recovering from eating disorders, helping them understand their conditions and develop coping strategies.", "REVISIÓN DENTAL:Dental check-ups are recommended for patients with Bulimia Nervosa to monitor and address dental health issues caused by vomiting."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}